  "id": "DrugBank_DB01176 - MONDO_grouped_11786_5324_24332",
  "verbalization": "Cyclizine, a medication primarily used for its antihistaminic properties, is linked through multiple pathways to Allergic Rhinitis. The evidence suggests that Cyclizine is associated with Vasomotor Rhinitis, a condition characterized by inflammation of the nasal mucosa, often triggered by factors other than allergens, such as colds or vasomotor stimuli. This connection is further supported by the indication of Mizolastine and Ramatroban, both of which are antihistaminic agents, leading to a chain of indications ultimately pointing to Allergic Rhinitis. The shared mechanism of action—targeting histamine receptors—underlines the potential for Cyclizine to influence allergic responses. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of Cyclizine in modulating inflammatory processes linked to allergic rhinitis, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
